BrandIcons bundles brand marks from three upstream sets. The code in this repository is
MIT. The marks are not the code, and they carry their own terms.

  Simple Icons 16.28.0   CC0-1.0    https://github.com/simple-icons/simple-icons
  theSVG Color                            MIT        https://thesvg.org
  SVG Logos (gilbarbara)                  CC0-1.0    https://github.com/gilbarbara/logos

4309 marks are compiled in, 3175 of them with full colour artwork.

TRADEMARK

CC0 and MIT waive copyright in the drawing. Neither touches trademark. CC0 says so itself, in
section 4(a):

  "No trademark or patent rights held by Affirmer are waived, abandoned, surrendered, licensed
   or otherwise affected by this document."

Drawing a company's logo in your interface is a trademark question, not a copyright one, and this
package cannot answer it for you. Using a mark to identify the company it belongs to is ordinarily
fine. Using one to imply endorsement, or as part of your own branding, is not.

MARKS WITH TERMS BEYOND CC0

223 marks record a licence other than the set default. Some forbid commercial use
or derivative works, which sits badly with a paid app and with what this package does to every
mark, which is reparse and rescale it.

  ResolverConfiguration(excludesRestrictiveLicenses = true)

leaves them out. The default is to include them, matching what the upstream sets ship, because
dropping marks silently would hide a decision that belongs to you.
